    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d770">

                <pb facs="0860" n="772" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg772"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Eddy.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-10-17"><hi rendition="#italic">October 17,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 157.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In connection with the Department’s
                    instruction No. 155, of the 13th instant, I inclose a bulletin of verification
                    issued under date of the 9th ultimo by the Japanese office at Nagasaki,
                    addressed to the office of San Francisco,<anchor n="a" xml:id="d770-f1"/>
                    reporting the opening and resealing by the Russian post-office at Vladivostok of
                    a sack made up at the office of San Francisco, addressed to the U. S. S. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cincinnati</hi> and dispatched per the steamer <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Calchas.</hi></p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
